  "standing": "PROPOSED C2b-1 inventory v244: 79 additive FILE rows for the files C2b-1a and C2b-1b add from main to the joint code head d2729979f0ff264711620f74b42fce84fb36e34c. Acceptances at their exact reviewed heads: C2B-FREEZE and C2B-PRIMITIVES-AUDIT at 9297fe5, carried to a03407d; C2B1A-CODE-r5 at fd697c1, carried to ca29d3c, 76ce532 and d272997; C2B1B-FUNDING at 9297fe5, fd697c1, ca29d3c and a03407d. OUTSTANDING: the C2b-1b funding carry and the freeze carry to the lock commit on d272997. Every v243 row, package and pending decision is unchanged. CARRIED (LD-Q-161-B/-D): The manual tools/check_package_edges.py already refuses main dd89db1 (opensip-launch, D1b, has no inventory package row; O1-a's policy admits only opensip-operability). This binding adds file rows only, so it refuses v243 and v244 alike at the head. The new crates opensip-host-law, opensip-host-metered and opensip-host-priced, and the crates/host-alloc-tests workspace's opensip-host-alloc-tests, get their package rows and the opensip-host edge update in PKG-ROWS-1 (a verify_design package-successor profile, LD-Q-161-B), which also covers opensip-launch so that check_package_edges passes on main (LD-Q-161-D).",
